From d94dd79252c65a6d4aa2b3543fd8e8f7b2106bd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:58:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vehicles): forward predicted boat and horse movement

Java sends vehicle position and paddle state separately from player movement. Bedrock's server-authoritative input expects the vehicle's predicted position, rotation, unique ID, and paddle flags while riding a client-predicted vehicle. Forward those fields and translate vehicle rewinds back into Java vehicle corrections so boats no longer operate on stale player coordinates.
---
